.SH DESCRIPTION
Run data transfer benchmarks between memories
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B
\fBxnvme-perf-xfer-htod\fP(1)
Keep \fB--qdepth\fP pinned copies of \fB--iosize\fP in flight to one GPU for \fB--runtime\fP
seconds and report the delivered host-to-device GB/s. Takes no NVMe devices.
.PP
.nf
.fam C
  xnvme-perf-xfer-register(1)  Register the dma-buf the process inherited as --dmabuf-fd with the device
.fam T
.fi
\fB--count\fP times, unregistering it after each, and report the microseconds
each call took. The dma-buf is named by addresses reserved with PROT_NONE,
which nothing reads or writes; its size is the exporter's. With \fB--homi-id\fP
the registrations go through the server.
.RE
.PP

